  <prompt>Implement lazy Contact attribution: on an internal (workforce) user's FIRST attributed action (e.g. submitting a request), resolve-or-create their Contact by workforce oid (reuse R1 `ResolveOrCreateContactAsync` + bind oid to `sprk_externalobjectid`) and record it as requester. No Contact is created merely by having access.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. BFF engineer fluent in the R1 Contact-provisioning machinery and idempotent resolve-or-create semantics.</role>
  <goal>The BFF resolves-or-creates a Contact by workforce oid on the first attributed action of a workforce user, binding oid to `sprk_externalobjectid` (semantics broadened to CIAM-or-workforce oid) and setting the Contact as requester. Second and subsequent actions reuse the same Contact. Having module access alone creates no Contact. Unit + KEEP-path integration tests cover create-once, reuse, and the no-Contact-on-access-only negative.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-11: on an internal user's first attributed action, the BFF resolves-or-creates a Contact by workforce oid (reuse R1 `ResolveOrCreateContact` + bind-oid to `sprk_externalobjectid`) and records it as requester. Acceptance: an employee's first submission creates/links exactly one Contact; subsequent actions reuse it; no Contact is created merely by having access. Spec Assumption: `sprk_externalobjectid` semantics broaden from "CIAM oid" to "external identity object id (CIAM OR workforce oid)" — one field, both planes (oids globally unique). MUST NOT create a Contact merely to grant internal access (entitlement = App Role; Contact = attribution, lazy).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/InviteExternalUserEndpoint.cs — `ResolveOrCreateContactAsync` :172 (reuse this; do NOT re-implement); oid → `sprk_externalobjectid` :139.</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalParticipationService.cs — resolve-by-oid :231 / bind-oid :323 (the canonical oid resolution/bind machinery).</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolver.cs — `CallerPrincipal` (:66) exposes `Oid` for the workforce plane; the attribution reads that oid.</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/module-entitlement-schema-decision.md — task 020 schema (attribution links requester Contact to the request record it will be set on, e.g. sprk_servicerequest requester in P3).</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>Task 021 (resolver) establishes the entitlement plane/principal. This attribution is invoked at the first attributed action (the P3 intake submit is a caller); the mechanism itself is delivered here so P3 wires it.</dependencies>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec-FR11">Resolve-or-create MUST be idempotent by oid: exactly one Contact per oid; a second attributed action reuses it (no duplicate). Reuse `ResolveOrCreateContactAsync` (:172) — do NOT re-implement Contact lookup/create. Scope: attribution path only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec-assumption">Broaden `sprk_externalobjectid` semantics to CIAM-OR-workforce oid (one field, both planes). Bind the workforce oid using the existing bind-oid machinery (:323 / :139). Scope: the field's usage in the workforce attribution path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec-MUST-NOT">MUST NOT create a Contact merely to grant internal access. Contact creation fires ONLY on a first attributed ACTION, never on entitlement/access alone. Scope: gating of the resolve-or-create call.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Placement Justification in the PR (cite `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`); `dotnet publish -c Release` compressed size + delta vs 46.90 MB baseline (≤60 MB); no new HIGH CVE; `/conflict-check` before the PR (teams-app-r1 shares this surface).</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
