    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="resolve-or-create-contact" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/InviteExternalUserEndpoint.cs">Reuse `ResolveOrCreateContactAsync` (:172) + oid bind (:139) — idempotent Contact provisioning by oid.</pattern>
      <pattern name="oid-bind" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalParticipationService.cs">resolve-by-oid (:231) / bind-oid (:323) — the canonical oid ↔ Contact machinery to reuse for the workforce plane.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Load spec FR-11 + the `sprk_externalobjectid`-broadening assumption + the MUST-NOT. Read `ResolveOrCreateContactAsync` (:172) and the oid bind machinery (:231/:323) to confirm reuse points.</step>
    <step order="2">Introduce an attribution service/method (e.g. `IContactAttributionService.EnsureRequesterContactAsync(CallerPrincipal)`) that: reads the workforce `Oid` from `CallerPrincipal`; calls the existing resolve-or-create-by-oid; binds oid to `sprk_externalobjectid`; returns the Contact id to set as requester. Reuse existing machinery — thin wrapper only.</step>
    <step order="3">Ensure the resolve-or-create is idempotent (one Contact per oid) and that the workforce oid path uses the same `sprk_externalobjectid` field (broadened semantics), not a new field.</step>
    <step order="4">Wire the attribution to be invoked from the first attributed action ONLY (the P3 intake-submit call site consumes this; do not call it from `/me` or entitlement resolution). Guard so access/entitlement alone never triggers it.</step>
    <step order="5">Register the service in DI (`ExternalAccessModule.cs`). ADR-010: only add an interface if a second impl or genuine test-seam is warranted; otherwise register the concrete.</step>
    <step order="6">Add unit + KEEP-path integration tests (ADR-038): first attributed action creates exactly one Contact bound to the oid; a second action reuses it (no duplicate); a caller who only has access but performs no attributed action → no Contact created (negative); an existing Contact already bound to that oid is reused not duplicated.</step>
    <step order="7">Build + test: `dotnet build` + `dotnet test`. Run `dotnet publish -c Release` and record compressed size + delta.</step>
    <step order="8">Run `/conflict-check`; write Placement Justification + publish-size delta into the PR/task notes.</step>
    <step order="9">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="10">Document any deviations in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a workforce oid collides with an existing CIAM-bound Contact on `sprk_externalobjectid` (same field, both planes), STOP — cross-plane identity collision is a security-sensitive case (email-hijack adjacency, FR-19) needing owner sign-off (§6) before choosing merge-vs-reject.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test/publish .NET</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Shell</tool>
  </tools>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ContactAttributionService.cs (thin reuse wrapper) + DI registration in ExternalAccessModule.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ + KEEP-path integration test for create-once / reuse / no-Contact-on-access-only</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a workforce user performing their first attributed action, when attribution runs, then exactly one Contact is created and bound to their oid via `sprk_externalobjectid`, and set as requester.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the same user performing a second attributed action, when attribution runs, then the existing Contact is reused (no duplicate created).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a user who has module access but performs no attributed action, when they browse, then NO Contact is created (negative — no Contact merely by access).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an oid already bound to a Contact, when attribution runs, then resolve-by-oid returns that Contact (idempotent by oid, not by email).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `dotnet publish -c Release`, when measured, then compressed size + delta vs 46.90 MB baseline is reported and ≤60 MB; BFF suite passes; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>This task delivers the MECHANISM; the P3 intake-submit endpoint is the first real caller. The field-broadening (CIAM-or-workforce oid on `sprk_externalobjectid`) is per spec Assumption — oids are globally unique so one field serves both planes. Reuse `ResolveOrCreateContactAsync`/bind-oid verbatim; this is not a re-implementation.</notes>
  <closure>
    <delivered-by>unified-access-control-r2 task 141 (GitHub #1064), "Workforce identity binding by Entra oid".</delivered-by>
    <summary>Delivered by unified-access-control-r2 task 141. The mechanism this task describes was built there as part of a wider identity-binding rewrite: a workforce caller binds to a contact by Entra oid in contact.sprk_externalobjectid (one field, both planes, plus a plane marker sprk_identityplane), with exactly one contact per oid (owner decision B2, UAC-r2 round 4 item 4: the alternate key sits on an unsecured mirror column sprk_externalobjectidkey written with the binding in one request, because Dataverse refuses a key on the field-secured binding; until the schema gate runs, contact creation denies and two contacts on one oid always deny — UAC-r2 notes/task-141-identity-binding.md §9). No ContactAttributionService was added. The writer is ContactIdentityBinder (Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ContactIdentityBinder.cs) and the read-side contract is projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/141-link-contract.md.</summary>
    <supersedes>Per owner round 2 item 4 and Q3 (unified-access-control-r2 session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md), a contact is created at the FIRST SIGN-IN of a member of a configured customer workforce tenant, not at the first attributed action. This supersedes FR-11's wording "no Contact is created merely by having access". The creation grants nothing: access still comes only from Dataverse (systemusers) or explicit grants (contacts). Acceptance criterion 3 of this task (no contact on access only) is therefore retired by owner decision, not met.</supersedes>
    <escalation-answered>The cross-plane collision trigger of this task was answered by the owner: refuse and flag, never merge and never re-bind (round 2 item 4; I2 = (1) for a licensed user's existing link).</escalation-answered>
    <remaining-with-spa-r2>The P3 intake-submit requester wiring stays with SPA-r2, as its consumer of this mechanism. It should take the requester from the resolved workforce principal's ContactId (WorkforcePrincipalResolution.ContactId) and must not resolve a contact by email. See notes/task-023-delivered-by-uac-r2-141.md.</remaining-with-spa-r2>
  </closure>
